A mixer base assembly for use with a mixing vessel, and a method of using the mixer base assembly, are disclosed. The mixer base assembly (500) comprises:
(a) a body (550) having:
(i) an upper end (571) including a mating face (575) for mixing vessel connection;
(ii) a lower end (572) including a cavity (557);
(iii) a plurality of side walls (551A, 551B, 551C, 551D);
(iv) an inlet port (501) arranged in a side wall;
(v) an outlet port (502) arranged in a side wall;
(vi) a sampling port (507) arranged in a side wall;
(vii) at least one probe port (518, 519) arranged in a side wall; and,
(viii) a fluid mixing chamber including a baffle (525), the fluid mixing chamber (530) having a bottom wall;
(b) an impeller seat (615) arranged in the cavity in the lower end of the body; and,
(c) a levitating magnetic impeller (650) arranged in the impeller seat, the impeller comprising a magnet, a base, and at least two blades, wherein the at least two blades extend above the bottom wall of the fluid mixing chamber into the fluid mixing chamber.

